      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ba5d139dabace1d8df9df6f|full_name}: While I can agree that searchable avatars can cause issues with semi-private or hidden avatars. I feel that limited avatar favorites actully stop people from exploring avatar worlds\nBefore avatar favorites existed (and to a point, before it was bumped to 16) I almost never went to avatar worlds, why would I, if I changed avatar, I couldn't change back. (and this is why I took up avatar creation within a week of playing the game)\nThe 16 avatar favourites we have now, improved the situation, but 16 avatars still isn't a lot (It's not uncommon to have a single avatar world with more avatars, not that I would go favorite all of them if I could) and you quickly run it not the situation of \"I have these avatars I want to keep, so there is no point going into avatar worlds anymore\"\nTLDR, limited Avatar favorites to encourage exploring avatar worlds is probable having the opersite effect.\nUnlimited Avatar favorites arn't the only thing clients have that the base game should, another feature I've been told they have is per user volume control. This is literally the top request (https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/adjust-volume-of-individuals), having over 20% more votes than the next most upvoted request. If there was ever an argument for devs ignoring the community, that one canny would be a strong one.\nI have trouble understanding quiter players (I.e. they have to keep quite to prevent waking anyone up), particuly in busy rooms and being able to boost their volume on my end would help alot.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
