  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "For a game about creating communities, I do not see the negatives for banning individuals for having \"modified clients.\" There are tons of benefits when it comes to mods, for example play space. Play space allows for people to lower and raise their avatar to a certain height without causing any discomfort to the headset user. Another one (the one I had gotten banned for) is avatar searching and unlimited avatar favorites. Which in my opinion should've already been in the game from the start, plus it saves people TONS of time from jumping to and from worlds in an attempt to find an avatar that is not too lewd or broken. Anyhow, to end my little cry baby rant of me being temp banned, mods help communities not destroy them.",
